# DTF tier manifest: otlp-upstream-client-spans  (artifact-keeper#3954, #4931; 1.12.0)
# Profile-set: filesystem + telemetry.otlp-spans (OTLP http/protobuf export to
# the stdlib sink of bind-ip-and-otel, which decodes every span to a JSON line
# with typed attribute values) + upstreams.mock-recorder (a file-table upstream
# at 172.16.<slot>.77 the oracle fills over its control port). The oracle
# recreates the backend once with fixtures/backend.tracing.yml
# (DB_QUERY_SPANS=all). A sibling of bind-ip-and-otel (request spans) and
# otlp-logs-metrics (log records and metrics); this tier gates the CLIENT
# spans of upstream requests and of SQL statements.
#
# Every request the oracle sends carries its own traceparent
# 00-<tid>-<sid>-01, so the spans of that request are the exported spans with
# trace_id <tid> (the default sampler honours the sampled flag, and the empty
# RATE_LIMIT_TRUSTED_PROXY_CIDRS accepts the header from any client).
#
# THE GATES
#   (CONTROL)  spans arrive; the http_request span of a request joins its
#              traceparent. Both images.
#   (FIX #3954, integer attributes) a generic Remote download fetched from the
#              mock exports a CLIENT span (kind 3) in the request's trace whose
#              url.full is the mock URL, http.response.status_code is the
#              INTEGER 200 and server.port the INTEGER 80. RED on 1.11.5: the
#              span exists (the proxy went through send_upstream in 1.11.0) but
#              both values are exported as strings ("200", "80").
#   (FIX #3954, test-upstream) POST /api/v1/repositories/<remote>/test-upstream
#              exports a CLIENT HEAD span to the remote's upstream URL in the
#              request's trace, with the integer status the mock answered.
#              RED on 1.11.5: a bare send, no span.
#   (FIX #3954, curation sync) POST /api/v1/curation/repos/<staging>/sync over
#              RPM repodata the mock serves runs one curation sync cycle; it
#              exports a CLIENT GET span for repodata/repomd.xml and one for
#              the primary it names, each with the integer status 200, and the
#              sync ingests the repodata's packages. RED on 1.11.5: no span.
#   (FIX #3954, DB_QUERY_SPANS=all) with RUST_LOG=info (sqlx::query at info,
#              which passes only slow statements) an authenticated request
#              exports at least one database CLIENT span
#              (db.system.name=postgresql) in its trace, and stdout still shows
#              no statement text (no db.statement field). RED on 1.11.5: no
#              DB span without sqlx::query=debug.
#
# NOT GATED HERE: the scheduled (5-minute) curation tick, which runs the same
# cycle outside any request, and the pypistats / npm popularity lookups, which
# go to fixed public hosts (both are covered by backend unit tests); the
# parallel exporter shutdown of #4931, whose guard lives in otlp-logs-metrics.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: two logins and a few dozen calls.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem telemetry.otlp-spans upstreams.mock-recorder"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS="true"
